Author: Wan-Teh Chang <wtc@google.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 6 12:31:17 2018 -0700

    Zero frame buffers on sequence header change.

    This improves the commit d63da28bf141d7025b6d9038e042befb6419fa65, which
    zeros the frame buffer every time aom_realloc_frame_buffer() is called.
    We only need to zero the unused internal frame buffers (which are
    waiting to be reused) after a sequence header change.

    Add the reproducer test cases for oss-fuzz:10061 and oss-fuzz:10227 to
    InvalidFileTest.

    Tested:
    ./test_libaom --gtest_filter=*InvalidFileTest*

    BUG=oss-fuzz:10061
    BUG=oss-fuzz:10227

    Change-Id: Idc24eb0e057268935efacd8cdeb89afee8d40eba

